<figure class="chapter-visual gzero-map">
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创示意图：整体中性、G=0 模式与周期 Coulomb 能</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original diagram: charge neutrality, the G=0 mode, and periodic Coulomb energy</span>
  </figcaption>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 920 380" role="img" aria-labelledby="gzero-title gzero-desc">
    <title id="gzero-title">Neutral and charged periodic cells in reciprocal-space electrostatics</title>
    <desc id="gzero-desc">
      A neutral periodic cell has zero total charge, so the Fourier coefficient rho at G equals zero vanishes and the reciprocal Coulomb sum can exclude the potential-reference mode. A charged cell has nonzero rho zero and the Coulomb term grows as one over G squared unless a compensating background and boundary convention are introduced.
    </desc>
    <defs>
      <marker id="gzero-arrow" markerWidth="9" markerHeight="9" refX="8" refY="4.5" orient="auto">
        <path d="M0,0 L9,4.5 L0,9 z" class="gzero-map__arrowhead" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <g transform="translate(35 42)">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="365" height="135" rx="12" class="gzero-map__box gzero-map__box--neutral" />
      <text x="182" y="30" text-anchor="middle">neutral cell: Q = ∫Ωρ dr = 0</text>
      <circle cx="90" cy="78" r="23" class="gzero-map__positive" />
      <text x="90" y="84" text-anchor="middle">+</text>
      <circle cx="275" cy="78" r="23" class="gzero-map__negative" />
      <text x="275" y="84" text-anchor="middle">−</text>
      <text x="182" y="119" text-anchor="middle">ρG=0 = Q = 0</text>
    </g>

    <g transform="translate(520 42)">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="365" height="135" rx="12" class="gzero-map__box gzero-map__box--charged" />
      <text x="182" y="30" text-anchor="middle">charged cell: Q ≠ 0</text>
      <circle cx="120" cy="78" r="23" class="gzero-map__positive" />
      <text x="120" y="84" text-anchor="middle">+</text>
      <circle cx="245" cy="78" r="23" class="gzero-map__positive" />
      <text x="245" y="84" text-anchor="middle">+</text>
      <text x="182" y="119" text-anchor="middle">ρG=0 = Q ≠ 0</text>
    </g>

    <line x1="218" y1="195" x2="218" y2="245" marker-end="url(#gzero-arrow)" class="gzero-map__arrow" />
    <line x1="702" y1="195" x2="702" y2="245" marker-end="url(#gzero-arrow)" class="gzero-map__arrow" />

    <g transform="translate(35 260)">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="365" height="88" rx="12" class="gzero-map__box" />
      <text x="182" y="30" text-anchor="middle">EC = (2π/Ω) ΣG≠0 |ρG|²/G²</text>
      <text x="182" y="60" text-anchor="middle">G=0 fixes potential reference; finite for smooth neutral ρ</text>
    </g>

    <g transform="translate(520 260)">
      <rect x="0" y="0" width="365" height="88" rx="12" class="gzero-map__box gzero-map__box--charged" />
      <text x="182" y="30" text-anchor="middle">EC(G→0) ~ 2πQ²/(ΩG²)</text>
      <text x="182" y="60" text-anchor="middle">requires background + boundary convention, not mere deletion</text>
    </g>
  </svg>

  <div class="gzero-map__fallback">
    <dl>
      <div><dt>中性周期胞 | Neutral cell</dt><dd><code>Q=ρ(G=0)=0</code>；<code>G=0</code> 只剩 potential zero/boundary 选择。</dd></div>
      <div><dt>带电周期胞 | Charged cell</dt><dd><code>Q≠0</code> 时 reciprocal Coulomb energy 以 <code>Q²/G²</code> 发散；必须声明 compensating background 与 macroscopic boundary。</dd></div>
      <div><dt>点电荷 | Point charges</dt><dd>即使整体中性，高 <code>G</code> 仍含 self divergence；Ewald split 负责分离并减去 self term。</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <dl lang="en">
      <div><dt>Neutral periodic cell</dt><dd><code>Q=ρ(G=0)=0</code>; the <code>G=0</code> mode reduces to a potential-zero and boundary choice.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Charged periodic cell</dt><dd>For <code>Q≠0</code>, reciprocal Coulomb energy diverges as <code>Q²/G²</code>; a compensating background and macroscopic boundary must be declared.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Point charges</dt><dd>Even in a neutral cell, high <code>G</code> contains a self divergence; the Ewald split isolates and subtracts the self term.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>学习目的：</strong>区分 potential reference、整体中性、均匀背景和点电荷 self term，避免把“删除 G=0”写成通用物理修正。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Learning purpose:</strong> separate the potential reference, global neutrality, uniform background, and point-charge self term so that “delete G=0” is not treated as a universal physical correction.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong>图与语义列表都必须给出 neutral/charged 两条路径，并写出 charged small-G 的 <code>1/G²</code> 发散。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> the diagram and semantic list both show neutral and charged paths and state the charged small-<code>G</code> <code>1/G²</code> divergence.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>图只表示三维周期 Fourier electrostatics。二维 cutoff、isolated boundary、finite dielectric boundary 和 surface term 需另行指定。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> the diagram represents three-dimensional periodic Fourier electrostatics only. Two-dimensional cutoffs, isolated boundaries, finite-dielectric boundaries, and surface terms require separate declarations.</p>
  </div>
</figure>

